# SchemeMatch AI

**"Right Scheme. Right Entrepreneur. Right Opportunity."**

Smart India Hackathon Prototype — Problem Statement **SIH26092**
Team **Protocol 6.9** · Karnavati University

SchemeMatch AI is an explainable, rule-based government scheme discovery platform.
An entrepreneur fills in a short profile, and the matching engine compares it against
a prototype scheme dataset, scores every scheme, and explains — in plain language —
why each one was (or wasn't) recommended.

---

## 1. Project overview

- Entrepreneur enters age, gender, category, state, income, business type, stage and funding need.
- The backend scores every scheme in `schemes.csv` against that profile using a transparent, weighted rule engine (not a black-box ML model).
- Results are ranked, labeled (Highly Relevant / Good Match / Potential Match), and explained with human-readable reasons and a document checklist.
- A single Python process starts the whole application, including — best effort — a supporting Java validation service.

## 2. Technology stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Backend / web server | Python 3 + Flask |
| Matching engine | Python (`matcher.py`) |
| Frontend | HTML5, CSS3, vanilla JavaScript |
| Supporting service | Java (built-in `com.sun.net.httpserver`, no frameworks) |
| Data | `schemes.csv` (prototype/demo data) |

No database server, no API keys, no cloud services, no Docker.

## 3. Architecture

```
USER
  ↓
HTML / CSS / JavaScript  (templates/, static/)
  ↓
FLASK  (app.py)
  ↓
PROFILE VALIDATION  →  Java service (java/SchemeService.java) if available,
                        otherwise an equivalent Python fallback in app.py
  ↓
MATCHING ENGINE  (matcher.py)
  ↓
SCHEME DATASET  (schemes.csv)
  ↓
RANKING + EXPLANATIONS
  ↓
RESULTS PAGE  (templates/results.html)
```

`app.py` is the **single entry point**. On startup it:
1. Starts the Flask web server.
2. Loads the scheme dataset via `matcher.py`.
3. Attempts to compile (if needed) and launch the Java validation service as a background process, polling briefly to confirm it came up.
4. If Java can't be found, can't compile, or doesn't respond in time, it logs a warning and the whole app keeps running in **fallback mode** — Java is never required for the site to work.
5. Serves the full frontend at `http://127.0.0.1:5000`.

## 4. Installation (Windows)

```
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

A JDK is optional — only needed if you want the live Java validation service instead of fallback mode. `javac -version` in your terminal tells you if one is installed.

## 5. How to run

```
python app.py
```

You'll see:

```
SchemeMatch AI
Running at http://127.0.0.1:5000
Java validation service: ONLINE / UNAVAILABLE (...)
```

Open **http://127.0.0.1:5000** in your browser. That's it — one command, one running application.

## 6. How Java integration works

`java/SchemeService.java` is a small HTTP service (Java's built-in `com.sun.net.httpserver`, no external libraries) that validates and normalizes a submitted profile — checking that gender, category, business type, stage and state are all recognized values, and that age/income/funding are sensible numbers.

`app.py` calls it over HTTP at `http://127.0.0.1:8080/validate`. If that call fails for any reason (service not running, JDK missing, timeout), `app.py` immediately falls back to an identical validation routine written in Python — the user never sees a difference except a status indicator in the **About** section of the site.

You never need to start Java yourself; `python app.py` attempts to compile and launch it automatically. If you want to run it manually for testing:

```
cd java
javac SchemeService.java
java SchemeService
```

## 7. How the matching algorithm works

`matcher.py` implements an **explainable, rule-based weighted scoring engine** — not a trained machine-learning model. Every scheme is scored out of 100:

| Factor | Points |
|---|---|
| Category match | 25 |
| Gender match | 15 |
| Business type match | 20 |
| State match | 10 |
| Income compatibility | 10 |
| Business stage match | 10 |
| Funding compatibility | 10 |

Each point awarded (or withheld) generates a human-readable reason, so every score is fully explainable. These are **prototype scoring weights only** and do not represent official government eligibility rules.

## 8. Using the demo profile

Click **Try Demo Profile** on the form to auto-fill: Age 28, Female, SC, Gujarat, Income ₹3,00,000, Tailoring, New Business, Funding ₹2,00,000. Then click **Find My Schemes →**.

## 9. Presenting to judges (under 60 seconds)

1. Show the landing page and AI preview card.
2. Click **Try Demo Profile**, then **Find My Schemes →** — narrate the short loading sequence.
3. Point out the ranked results, match scores, and "Why this matches" reasons.
4. Open **View Details** on the top match to show the full explanation and documents.
5. Scroll to **About** and show the System Status card — explain Python, the matching engine, and Java's supporting role (and that Java failure never breaks the site).
6. Close on the disclaimer: this is an indicative prototype, not official eligibility.

## 10. Important notes

- All scheme data in `schemes.csv` is prototype/demo data. Where an official source isn't verified, the UI says so explicitly.
- Match scores are indicative only and are displayed with that disclaimer throughout the site.
- No submitted profile data is stored — each request is processed in-memory for that session only.